{ HotOps.inc - which opcodes src/hotdisp.c implements. GENERATED from that file: the two must not
  drift, because a mismatch either calls C for an opcode it cannot run (a wasted call per
  instruction) or skips C for one it can (a silent loss of the whole point).

  The interpreter uses this to avoid CALLING the C loop for an instruction it would refuse: without
  it, a program whose hot loop mixes covered and uncovered opcodes pays one call per uncovered one,
  which measured +20% on n-body and +13% on spectral-norm - both array-heavy, and arrays are not
  covered yet. }
